# .sgl/allowed-licenses — the dependency license allow-list for THIS repo.
# One SPDX id or glob per line. Case-insensitive. Blank lines and # comments ignored.
# A line starting with "!" is an explicit DENY that overrides any allow (and overrides
# the fallback-allow mode). The allow-list file is governance (.sgl/*): editing it is R3.
#
# check-licenses.sh reads this file. Any dependency whose license is NOT allowed here
# fails CI. An unknown/undeterminable license fails too (treated as disallowed).
#
# ---- Choose the posture for this repo (keep ONE block) ----
#
# POSTURE A — permissive open-source repo (e.g. the public harness, MIT):
MIT
Apache-2.0
BSD-2-Clause
BSD-3-Clause
ISC
0BSD
Unlicense
Python-2.0
Zlib
#
# POSTURE B — proprietary / closed repo (the private swarm product):
# use ONLY the allows below and keep the copyleft denies. Delete Posture A above.
# MIT
# Apache-2.0
# BSD-2-Clause
# BSD-3-Clause
# ISC
# 0BSD
# !GPL-*
# !LGPL-*
# !AGPL-*
# !MPL-*
# !EPL-*
# !CDDL-*
# !SSPL-*
# !BUSL-*
#
# A copyleft exception (proprietary repo) is a Human-Steward-recorded, lawyer-cleared
# decision — add it as an explicit allow with a comment, e.g.:
#   LGPL-2.1-only   # approved <name> <date>: dynamically linked, not distributed; see TICKET-123
